[{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Sketch the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=-1,c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on a single set of axes.</p>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p1-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Sketch the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1x+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=-1,c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on a single set of axes.</p><h3><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\mathrm f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></h3>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p1-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>For what value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the gradient zero?</p></li><li><p>Find the general solution to the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions represented by the general solution on a single set of axes.</p></li><li><p>Describe how the family of solutions are related geometrically.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The gradient is zero when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\\Rightarrow2x=0\\Rightarrow x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=x^2+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p2-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>The family of solutions are vertical translations of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\cos x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the general solution to the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions represented by the general solution on a single set of axes.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\cos x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=\\sin x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p2-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q5","number":5,"question":"<h3>Separation of Variables</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3y\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=Ae^{3x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant.</p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions represented by the general solution when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on a single set of axes.</p></li><li><p>Describe what happens as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3y\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\int\\frac1y\\,dy=\\int3\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\ln|y|=3x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=\\pm e^{3x+c}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=\\pm e^{3x}e^c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=Ae^{3x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p3-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty,y\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis is a horizontal asymptote)</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q6","number":6,"question":"<h3>Separation of Variables</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Determine the constant solution to the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Find the general solution to the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions represented by the general solution on a single set of axes.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2,\\frac{dy}{dx}=2-2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and so is a constant solution to the differential equation.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\int\\frac1{y-2}\\,dy=\\int dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\ln|y-2|=x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y-2=\\pm e^{x+c}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=2\\pm e^xe^c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=2+Ae^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p4-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q7","number":7,"question":"<h3>Separation of Variables</h3><p>Solve each of these differential equations and hence sketch the family of solutions.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-2y\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=1-y\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac1{2y},\\quad y&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Q8: A-Level Maths Partial Fractions</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-2y\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\int\\frac1y\\,dy=\\int-2\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\ln|y|=-2x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=\\pm e^{-2x+c}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=\\pm e^{-2x}e^c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=Ae^{-2x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p4-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=1-y\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\int\\frac1{1-y}\\,dy=\\int dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow-\\ln|1-y|=x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\ln|1-y|=k-x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow1-y=\\pm e^{k-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=1\\pm e^ke^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=1+Ae^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p5-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\int\\frac1{y^2}\\,dy=\\int dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow-\\frac1y=x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac1y=A-x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=\\frac1{A-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p5-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac1{2y}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\int2y\\,dy=\\int dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y^2=x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=\\pm\\sqrt{x+c}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y&gt;0,y=\\sqrt{x+c}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p6-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q8","number":8,"question":"<h3>Separation of Variables</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y(1-y)\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Determine the constant solutions to the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Use separation of variables to show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{Ae^x}{1+Ae^x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Explain why one of the constant solutions from part a) does not appear in the solution found in part b).</p></li><li><p>Show that the solution in b) can also be written in the form</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{1+Be^{-x}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Explain why the other constant solution from part a) does not appear in the solution found in part d).</p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions represented by the solutions in parts a) and b) on a single set of axes.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0,\\frac{dy}{dx}=0(1-0)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1,\\frac{dy}{dx}=1(1-1)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constant solutions to the differential equation.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y(1-y)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\int\\frac1{y(1-y)}\\,dy=\\int dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Use Partial Fractions:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac1{y(1-y)}\\equiv\\frac Ay+\\frac B{1-y}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow1\\equiv A(1-y)+By\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0:1=A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1:1=B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\frac1{y(1-y)}\\equiv\\frac1y+\\frac1{1-y}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\int\\left(\\frac1y+\\frac1{1-y}\\right)\\,dy=\\int dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\ln|y|-\\ln|1-y|=x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\ln\\left|\\frac y{1-y}\\right|=x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac y{1-y}=\\pm e^{x+c}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac y{1-y}=\\pm e^xe^c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac y{1-y}=Ae^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=Ae^x-Ae^xy\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y+Ae^xy=Ae^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow(1+Ae^x)y=Ae^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=\\frac{Ae^x}{1+Ae^x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>In part a), we found <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constant solutions of the differential equation.</p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"0=\\frac{Ae^x}{1+Ae^x}\\Rightarrow A=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1=\\frac{Ae^x}{1+Ae^x}\\Rightarrow1+Ae^x=Ae^x\\Rightarrow1=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> does not appear in the solution found in part b), but <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> does.</p>","<p>When we separate the variables from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y(1-y)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\int\\frac1{y(1-y)}\\,dy=\\int dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span> we are assuming <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\neq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\neq1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y =\\frac{Ae^x}{1+Ae^x}=\\frac{\\frac{Ae^x}{Ae^x}}{\\frac1{Ae^x}+\\frac{Ae^x}{Ae^x}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =\\frac1{\\frac1Ae^{-x}+1}=\\frac1{1+Be^{-x}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>In part a), we found <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constant solutions of the differential equation.</p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"0=\\frac1{1+Be^{-x}}\\Rightarrow0=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1=\\frac1{1+Be^{-x}}\\Rightarrow1+Be^{-x}=1\\Rightarrow B=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> does not appear in the solution found in part d), but <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> does.</p>","<p>When we separate the variables from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=y(1-y)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\int\\frac1{y(1-y)}\\,dy=\\int dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span> we are assuming <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\neq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\neq1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p8-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q9","number":9,"question":"<h3>Integrating Factors</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the constant solution of the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Use an integrating factor to solve the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions on a single set of axes.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Trial:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=k\\Rightarrow \\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore0+k=3\\Rightarrow k=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant solution of the differential equation.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Integrating Factor</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=e^{\\int1\\,dx}=e^{x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^{x}\\frac{dy}{dx}+e^xy=3e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^{x}y)=3e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^{x}y=3e^x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=3+ce^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p9-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q10","number":10,"question":"<h3>Integrating Factors</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the constant solution of the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Solve the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Describe the behaviour of solutions as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions on a single set of axes.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Trial:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=k\\Rightarrow \\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore0-k=2\\Rightarrow k=-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant solution of the differential equation.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Integrating Factor</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=e^{\\int-1\\,dx}=e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^{-x}\\frac{dy}{dx}-e^{-x}y=2e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^{-x}y)=2e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^{-x}y=-2e^{-x}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=-2+ce^{x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty,e^x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p11-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q11","number":11,"question":"<h3>Integrating Factors</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+2y=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the constant solution of the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Solve the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Describe the behaviour of solutions as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions on a single set of axes.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Q12-Q15: Reversing the Chain Rule, Integration by Parts</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Trial:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=k\\Rightarrow \\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore0+2k=6\\Rightarrow k=3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant solution of the differential equation.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+2y=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Integrating Factor</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=e^{\\int2\\,dx}=e^{2x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+2y=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^{2x}\\frac{dy}{dx}+2e^{2x}y=6e^{2x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^{2x}y)=6e^{2x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^{2x}y=3e^{2x}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=3+ce^{-2x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty,e^{-2x}\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p12-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q12","number":12,"question":"<h3>Integrating Factors</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy=4x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Solve the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Describe the behaviour of the solutions as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions on a single set of axes.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Trial:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=k\\Rightarrow \\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore0+2x\\times k=4x\\Rightarrow k=2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant solution of the differential equation.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy=4x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Integrating Factor</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=e^{\\int2x\\,dx}=e^{x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xy=4x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^{x^2}\\frac{dy}{dx}+2xe^{x^2}y=4xe^{x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^{x^2}y)=4xe^{x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^{x^2}y=2e^{x^2}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=2+ce^{-x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty,e^{-x^2}\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So every solution curve tends to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> tends to infinity</p>","<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty,e^{-x^2}\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So every solution curve tends to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> tends to negative infinity</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p13-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q13","number":13,"question":"<h3>Integrating Factors</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=x+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use an integrating factor to show that the general solution is</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x+Ae^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant.</p></li><li><p>Show that the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is itself a solution of the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Explain why every solution curve approaches the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions on a single set of axes.</p></li><li><p>Show that distinct solution curves do not intersect.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=x+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Integrating Factor</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=e^{\\int1\\,dx}=e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=x+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^x\\frac{dy}{dx}+e^xy=(x+1)e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^xy)=(x+1)e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Use Integration by Parts:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"u=x+1,\\quad\\frac{dv}{dx}=e^x,\\quad\\frac{du}{dx}=1,\\quad v=e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\int(x+1)e^x\\ln x\\,dx =(x+1)e^x-\\int e^x\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =xe^x+e^x-e^x+c=xe^x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore e^xy=xe^x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=x+ce^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+x=x+1,y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a solution of the differential equation.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty,e^{-x}\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So every solution curve approaches the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p15-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>Let one solution curve have equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x+c_1e^{-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and let another solution curve have equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x+c_2e^{-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c_1\\neq c_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If they were to intersect, then:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x+c_1e^{-x}=x+c_2e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow c_1e^{-x}=c_2e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow c_1=c_2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>But <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c_1\\neq c_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so the solution curves cannot intersect.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q14","number":14,"question":"<h3>Integrating Factors</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Solve the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Show that the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a solution of the differential equation.</p></li><li><p>Describe the behaviour of the solutions as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Describe the behaviour of the solutions as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions on a single set of axes.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Integrating Factor</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=e^{\\int-1\\,dx}=e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^{-x}\\frac{dy}{dx}-e^{-x}y=xe^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^{-x}y)=xe^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Use Integration by Parts:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"u=x,\\quad\\frac{dv}{dx}=e^{-x},\\quad\\frac{du}{dx}=1,\\quad v=-e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\int xe^{-x}\\,dx =-xe^{-x}+\\int e^{-x}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =-xe^{-x}-e^{-x}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore e^{-x}y=-xe^{-x}-e^{-x}+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=-x-1+ce^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x-1\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1-(-x-1)=x,y=-x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a solution of the differential equation.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty,e^x\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to-x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to-x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So every solution curve approaches the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty,e^x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So every solution curve diverges from the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, unless <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p17-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q15","number":15,"question":"<h3>Integrating Factors</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=\\sin x+\\cos x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Solve the differential equation to show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x+Ae^{-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Explain why every solution approaches the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions on a single set of axes.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Q16: Calculus with Hyperbolic Functions</strong></p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=\\sin x+\\cos x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Integrating Factor</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=e^{\\int1\\,dx}=e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=\\sin x+\\cos x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^x\\frac{dy}{dx}+e^xy=e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^xy)=e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"I=\\int e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Use Integration by Parts:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"u=\\sin x+\\cos x,\\quad\\frac{dv}{dx}=e^x,\\quad\\frac{du}{dx}=\\cos x-\\sin x,\\quad v=e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore I=e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)-\\int e^x(\\cos x-\\sin x)\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Use Integration by Parts again:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"u=\\cos x-\\sin x,\\quad\\frac{dv}{dx}=e^x,\\quad\\frac{du}{dx}=-\\sin x-\\cos x,\\quad v=e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore I =e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)-\\left(e^x(\\cos x-\\sin x)-\\int e^x(-\\sin x-\\cos x)\\,dx\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow I =e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)-\\left(e^x(\\cos x-\\sin x)+\\int e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)\\,dx\\right)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow I =e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)-e^x(\\cos x-\\sin x)-\\int e^x(\\sin x+\\cos x)\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow I =e^x\\sin x+e^x\\cos x-e^x\\cos x+e^x\\sin x-I\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow2I =2e^x\\sin x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow I =e^x\\sin x+A\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\therefore e^xy =e^x\\sin x+A\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y =\\sin x+Ae^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty,e^{-x}\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\to\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So every solution curve approaches the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p19-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.40-q16","number":16,"question":"<h3>Integrating Factors</h3><p>It is given that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=4\\sinh x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Solve the differential equation to show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=e^x+(A-2x)e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant.</p></li><li><p>State the coordinates of the point where a solution curve crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Describe the behaviour of the solutions as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that the stationary points of the family of solution lie on the curve</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=4\\sinh x\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Sketch the family of solutions on a single set of axes.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=4\\sinh x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Integrating Factor</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=e^{\\int1\\,dx}=e^x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=4\\sinh x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^x\\frac{dy}{dx}+e^xy=4e^x\\sinh x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^xy)=4e^x\\sinh x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^xy)=4e^x\\times\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^xy)=2e^x(e^x-e^{-x})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac d{dx}(e^xy)=2e^{2x}-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^xy=e^{2x}-2x+A\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=e^x+(A-2x)e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y|_{x=0} =e^0+(A-2\\times0)e^0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =1+A\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So the solution curves intersect the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1+A)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to\\infty,e^{-x}\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"e^x\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So every solution curve tends to infinity as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> tends to infinity</p>","<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\to-\\infty,e^{-x}\\to\\infty\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"e^x\\to0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So every solution curve tends to infinity as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> tends to negative infinity</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=e^x+(A-2x)e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=e^x-(A-2x)e^{-x}-2e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Stationary points exist when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore e^x-(A-2x)e^{-x}-2e^{-x}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^x-Ae^{-x}+2xe^{-x}-2e^{-x}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow e^{2x}-A+2x-2=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow A=e^{2x}+2x-2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Substitute <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=e^{2x}+2x-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> into <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^x+(A-2x)e^{-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=e^x+((e^{2x}+2x-2)-2x)e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=e^x+(e^{2x}-2)e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=e^x+e^x-2e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=2e^x-2e^{-x}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=4\\times\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=4\\sinh x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively:</p>","<p>The original differential equation is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=4\\sinh x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Stationary points exist when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore0+y=4\\sinh x\\Rightarrow y=4\\sinh x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.40/solutions/assets/diagrams/240-p21-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]}]